  "construction": "Surface code of the orientably-regular map C50.3 of type {6,6} (genus 50) in M. Conder's list of chiral maps of genus 2 to 301, in its mirror image (Conder's relators hold for (r^-1, s^-1); mirror images give the same code). Rotation group G = <r,s | r^6, s^6, (r*s)^2, r^-1*s*r^-1*s*r^-3*s*r^-1*s^-3> of order 588. Darts = elements of G (right multiplication), faces = cosets g<r>, vertices = cosets g<s>, edges = cosets g<rs> = {g, grs}. Qubits on the 294 edges, X-checks on the 98 vertices (weight 6), Z-checks on the 98 faces (weight 6), incidences mod 2: H_X and H_Z are the boundary maps of the cellular chain complex over F_2, k = 2 - chi = 100, d_Z is the shortest homologically nontrivial cycle of the map and d_X that of the dual map. Found in a census of regular maps (normal subgroups of the triangle groups <r,s | r^p, s^q, (rs)^2>, Magma's LowIndexNormalSubgroups). The qubit order is that of the dart permutations in the public package in the references (data/maps.json), whose src/rebuild.py rebuilds these matrices from them and from the presentation.",
